    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2906eeb8-ae24-5ffa-ab14-ba5211384948",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $10\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{7}\\right)-5$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&10\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{7}\\right)-5\\\\&=5\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{7}\\right)-1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{13\\pi}{7}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{7}\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi}{7}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{26\\pi}{7}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{7}\\right)-1\\right)&=5\\cos\\left(\\frac{26\\pi}{7}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
