      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $2\\sqrt{3}\\cos^2\\left(59^\\circ\\right)-\\sqrt{3}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&2\\sqrt{3}\\cos^2\\left(59^\\circ\\right)-\\sqrt{3}\\\\&=\\sqrt{3}\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(59^\\circ\\right)-1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=59^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(59^\\circ\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 59^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(118^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt{3}\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(59^\\circ\\right)-1\\right)&=\\sqrt{3}\\cos\\left(118^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
